[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### 1. Broken stdout pipe: exit 0 instead of death by SIGPIPE
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **Symptom**: with stdout connected to a pipe whose reader has already exited,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the C program is terminated by `SIGPIPE` (shell status 141) while the Rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   program exited 0. stdout and stderr were identical (both empty), so a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   stdout-only comparison passed and hid the difference.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   $ { sleep 0.5; echo 42; } | c_src/build/driver | true      # -> 141
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   $ { sleep 0.5; echo 42; } | translation/.../driver | true  # -> 0   (wrong)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **Cause**: the Rust standard library sets `SIGPIPE` to `SIG_IGN` before
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   entering `main`. A failing write therefore returns `EPIPE` instead of killing
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the process, and the translation discards write errors (`let _ = write!(...)`)
